      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nThe ROCm 10.1 MI45x image (`rocm/sgl-dev:*-rocm101-mi45x-*`) is built without MORI, so the MORI tests (`test_umbp_store.py`, `test_mori_backend_basic.py`) fail on it with `No module named 'mori'`.\r\n\r\nMORI was turned off because it used to need `rocm_smi`, which ROCm 10.1 no longer ships (only `amd_smi`). The MORI version we pin (`f39fa765`) already switches to `amd_smi` on ROCm 10.1, so it can be turned back on.\r\n\r\nWhile testing, two problems in the CI install script also showed up for this image:\r\n- It didn't recognize the image's arch tag (`gfx1250-rocm1010`), guessed `gfx942` from the runner name, and installed the wrong Python extras (not the torch 2.12 set).\r\n- When a PR bumps `MORI_COMMIT`, it rebuilt MORI for a GPU arch guessed from the runner name (`gfx942` unless MI35x), replacing the correct gfx1250 build in MI45x images.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- `.github/workflows/release-docker-amd-rocm10.yml`: build the ROCm 10.1 gfx1250 image with `ENABLE_MORI=1`, same as the ROCm 10.0 one.\r\n- `scripts/ci/amd/amd_ci_install_dependency.sh`:\r\n  - Recognize `-rocm1010` images and install `dev_hip_rocm101` extras for them.\r\n  - Rebuild MORI for the arch stamped in the image (`IMAGE_GFX`) instead of guessing from the runner name.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nNo change to model outputs. Tested on an MI450X (gfx1250) with ROCm 10.1, on top of `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.22-rocm101-mi45x-20261026`: the Dockerfile's MORI step builds unchanged in ~3 minutes, then:\r\n\r\n| Test | Result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_umbp_store.py` | 14 passed |\r\n| `test/registered/amd/disaggregation/test_mori_backend_basic.py` | 6 passed |\r\n\r\n<!-- Full image build from this branch (job_select=publish-gfx1250-rocm101, push=false): run link -->\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nN/A.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40471684341](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40471684341)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40471684460](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40471684460)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD 